VALUES (
  '2026/08/31/hdq-month-august-2026',
  'month', 'month',
  'The Month Gold Miners Carried the TSX to Eight Records While Oil Went Nowhere', 'Gold miners lifted the TSX 2.7% and eight record closes while Brent finished the month 0.4% higher after a US$15 round trip. Financials and utilities fell, Canadian yields rose with no Bank of Canada decision, and a hawkish Federal Reserve chair helped take 4.6% off gold from its August 24 peak.',
  '<ul>
<li><strong>The TSX rose 2.7% in August to close at 36,180.72 after eight record closes,</strong><span> the last on August 25 at 36,957.63, and finished the month 2.1% below that record after the final four sessions.</span></li>
<li><strong>Gold futures gained 9.1% to US$4,481.50 and the gold miners ETF gained 32.1%,</strong><span> while financials fell 3.2% and utilities 5.9%, so the index record rested on a narrow base.</span></li>
<li><strong>Brent closed 0.4% higher after trading between US$79.36 and US$94.39,</strong><span> as WTI fell 11.2% in three sessions on Hormuz deal talk and then rose 16.8% as the deal talks stalled.</span></li>
<li><strong>The Bank of Canada held at 2.25% and the 2-year, 5-year and 10-year yields rose 10, 6 and 8 basis points,</strong><span> with the 10-year reaching 3.76% on August 21 before the trade talks collapsed.</span></li>
<li><strong>Canadian GDP grew at a 3.3% annualized pace in the second quarter against a Bank forecast of 2.5%,</strong><span> yet 50% US tariffs on about US$20 billion of goods took effect August 22 and markets priced roughly a 60% chance of a Fed hike on September 16.</span></li>
</ul>',
